          "filename": "Carved oak fence post at Castle Rising Castle - geograph.org.uk - 960555.jpg",
          "caption": "Carved oak fence post at Castle Rising, one of the largest, best preserved and most lavishly decorated keeps in England, surrounded by 20 acres of mighty earthworks. Begun in 1138 by William d'Albini for his new wife, the widow of Henry I, in the 14th century it became the luxurious exile-place of Queen Isabella, widow (and alleged murderess) of Edward II.",
